direction: down

title: |md
  ## TID vs TGID — pick the right key for in-flight tracking
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

proc: "Process firefox (TGID = 13421)" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  t1: "Thread 1\nTID 13421\n(also TGID leader)" {style.fill: "#dbeafe"}
  t2: "Thread 2\nTID 13422" {style.fill: "#dbeafe"}
  t3: "Thread 3\nTID 13423" {style.fill: "#dbeafe"}
  t4: "Thread 4\nTID 13424" {style.fill: "#dbeafe"}
}

scenario: |md
  ### Scenario: all 4 threads call vfs_read concurrently
| {shape: text}

wrong: "WRONG: key by TGID" {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
  body_w: |md
    Map: { 13421 → ts1 }

    Thread 1 enters → store ts1 with key 13421
    Thread 2 enters → **overwrite** ts2 with key 13421
    Thread 3 enters → **overwrite** ts3 with key 13421
    Thread 4 enters → **overwrite** ts4 with key 13421
    Thread 1 exits → reads ts4 (the most recent overwrite)

    → Latency = exit_time(t1) - entry_time(t4)
    → Garbage values, sometimes huge, sometimes negative
  |
}

right: "RIGHT: key by TID" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  body_r: |md
    Map: { 13421→ts1, 13422→ts2, 13423→ts3, 13424→ts4 }

    Each thread has its own slot
    Each exit retrieves *its* entry timestamp
    No collisions

    → Latency = exit(tN) - entry(tN) for each thread
    → Correct per-call duration
  |
}

proc -> wrong: "all 4 hit same map slot"
proc -> right: "each thread, own slot"

note: |md
  **Rule:** for synchronous per-thread tracking, key by **TID**.
  TID = lower 32 bits of `bpf_get_current_pid_tgid()`.
  TGID = upper 32 bits = what userspace calls "PID".
| {near: bottom-center; shape: text}
